{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"DISPOSITION CORRECTION (per plan-review G1G2/G6, applying principle #1's compose_config discriminator):\n\nThe plan-review gate correctly caught that freshness.py:80 and fsck_tracker_health.py (_branch_mismatch fallback, _tracker_sync_status, _configured_remote_ref) READ compose_config() — they call config.tickets_branch()/config.tickets_remote() which load rebar.toml. By the approved principle #1 (anything reading compose_config resolves the CODE root), these are CODE-ROOT sites, NOT store-root — identical in kind to reads.py:249. The operator's shorthand 'fsck_* = store root' pre-dated the observation that fsck_tracker_health's health probe reads tickets.branch/tickets.remote config; the principle governs the bucketing.\n\nCorrected dispositions:\n- CODE ROOT (config.repo_root_or_none(); behavior-changing on a relocated store; RED→GREEN in tests/unit/test_relocated_store_repo_root.py):\n  reads.py:238/:249/:374, freshness.py:80 (_remote_ref), fsck_tracker_health.py _branch_mismatch fallback / _tracker_sync_status / _configured_remote_ref. (_branch_mismatch still prefers the code repo_root fsck threads; only its None fallback moved from store-parent to code-root.)\n- STORE ROOT (shared seam rebar._proc.store_repo_root(); behavior-preserving; NO compose_config read):\n  _proc.py detached_child_cwd, compact_txn/rebuild _build_authorship_ledger (git history/signing), compact_plan attribution_fields (git identity/author_email), fsck.py:253 repo_guess (path-hint string joined to .tickets-tracker).\n- ALREADY SANCTIONED (str-form, untouched): sync.py:305/307.\n\nVerified: compact_* authorship/attribution helpers use repo_root for git-history/identity ops (_build_authorship_ledger, attribution_fields → author_email/resolve_current_identity), NOT compose_config; fsck.py:253 builds only a path string. So they are correctly behavior-preserving store-root. Only the 4 tickets_branch/tickets_remote readers changed behavior, each now with a RED→GREEN oracle."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787967543410789001,"uuid":"e027cc90-a097-4a10-bf14-adca7431c1c3"}